{"sentences": [{"sentence_id": "s1", "sentence": "Fourteen trials test BCMA CAR-T in myasthenia gravis, with one in Phase 3, two in Phase 2, and eleven in Phase 1.", "cites": ["NCT06419166"]}, {"sentence_id": "s2", "sentence": "Thirteen of the fourteen trials are currently running, and one was withdrawn before enrolling any participants.", "cites": ["NCT06419166"]}, {"sentence_id": "s3", "sentence": "Trials are sponsored by multiple institutions and companies, including Cartesian Therapeutics, Gilead, and academic centers.", "cites": ["NCT06419166"]}, {"sentence_id": "s4", "sentence": "Descartes-08, a BCMA-directed mRNA CAR-T therapy, was tested in multiple non-MG indications, with one Phase 1 multiple myeloma trial terminated after completion and another terminated due to sponsor decision.", "cites": ["NCT03448978", "NCT04816526"]}, {"sentence_id": "s6", "sentence": "A 2026 phase 2b randomized, double-blind, placebo-controlled trial showed that Descartes-08 significantly improved the MG Composite score at month 3 compared to placebo.", "cites": ["PMID:41514038"]}, {"sentence_id": "s7", "sentence": "The same trial reported that 66.7% of Descartes-08 recipients achieved a ≥5-point improvement in MGC score at month 3, versus 27.3% on placebo, with sustained improvement through month 12.", "cites": ["PMID:41514038"]}, {"sentence_id": "s8", "sentence": "Recent literature from 2025–2026 highlights durable clinical improvement and favorable safety in refractory MG patients treated with BCMA CAR-T therapies, including minimal toxicity and no severe cytokine release syndrome.", "cites": ["PMID:40856088", "PMID:41958278"]}, {"sentence_id": "s9", "sentence": "The median trial stop risk for BCMA CAR-T in MG is estimated at 13.7%, based on nine running trials.", "cites": ["RISK:bcma-car-t:MG"]}, {"sentence_id": "s10", "sentence": "Descartes-08 has demonstrated efficacy in an outpatient setting without lymphodepletion, differentiating it from conventional CAR-T approaches.", "cites": ["PMID:41514039"]}], "sources": [{"id": "NCT06419166", "text": "{"nct":"NCT06419166","title":"An Exploratory Clinical Study of GC012F Injection for Refractory gMG","state":"stopped","drug":"gc012f","start_year":2024,"end_year":2027,"phase":"EARLY_1","overall_status":"WITHDRAWN","why_stopped":"The study stopped early, before enrolling its first participant.","lead_sponsor":"Zhejiang University"}
